the type relies on implicit inheritance and is referenced before its declaration. This change initializes the type at its first declaration and preserves merging for later declarations. It adds five regression tests.

Fixes #136277.

A class or value type that relies on implicit inheritance and is referenced before its `.class` declaration was emitted with no base type, so the runtime refused to load it ("the parent does not exist"). The issue has the details, a repro, and the failures it causes in #136189's managed ilasm test build.

A reference created the type's entity before its first declaration. That declaration then took the merge path intended for later declarations. This path did not apply the implicit base type or check for unsealed value types. The fix initializes the type at its first declaration whether or not a reference created the entity first. A later declaration still merges. The synthetic `<Module>` type is marked declared when the registry creates it, so an explicit `.class '<Module>'` still merges and keeps its nil base type.

Tests, in `TypeDefinitionTests`:
- a class referenced before its declaration extends `System.Object`;
- a value type referenced before its declaration extends `System.ValueType`;
- a value type referenced before its declaration reports `UnsealedValueType` if the declaration extends `System.ValueType` without `sealed`;
- a second declaration of a generic type keeps one generic parameter, so a later declaration still merges;
- an explicit `.class '<Module>'` declaration keeps a nil base type.

`ILAssembler.Tests`: 5359 passed, 0 failed. Changing the fix to always merge makes the three forward-reference tests fail. Always initializing the type makes the generic redeclaration and `<Module>` tests fail. Never marking a type as declared makes the generic redeclaration test fail. Not marking `<Module>` as declared makes the `<Module>` test fail.

The following `src/tests` cases return 100 on the shared framework when assembled with this change: `Conv_I4`, `Conv_I8`, `Conv_R4`, `cpobj` (unaligned/1), `dev10_710121`, `nesting18` and `nesting31`. When assembled with the managed ilasm from `main`, they fail with the exception described in the issue.

> [!NOTE]
> This change was prepared with AI assistance (Anthropic Claude and OpenAI Codex) under my direction. AI agents ran the builds and tests on my machine. I reviewed the change and this description before posting.
